  /// <summary>A 1D finite-element mesh: a strictly increasing sequence of node coordinates. Element i spans [nodes[i], nodes[i+1]] for i in [0, num_elements()) -- no separate connectivity array is needed since consecutive nodes are always the two endpoints of one linear (P1) element. <c>nodes</c> is a public field for direct C++ construction, but (matching datamunge::ode::ODESolution's t/y fields -- a swig-jse R-backend codegen bug hits plain vector&lt;double&gt; struct *field* getters) is not exposed to language bindings; node_at()/num_nodes() are the cross-language-safe accessors.</summary>
