  /// <summary>Owned endpoint data for Dirichlet, outward-conormal Neumann or Robin conditions. Dirichlet uses value as u; Neumann uses it as p*du/dn; Robin uses it as the reference value in p*du/dn+alpha*(u-value)=0. Alpha zero gives zero conormal. For coercive diffusion/heat models use nonnegative Robin alpha and sufficient constraints/reaction to remove the constant nullspace. Unsupported enum values and nonfinite data are outside the solver's preconditions, not fully validated.</summary>
