  /// <summary>A two-predictor MLP classifier with Bayesian hidden-width selection and a held-out test.</summary>
  /// <remarks>
  /// <para>Wraps the C++ class <c>datamunge::MLPClassifierSearch</c>.</para>
  /// <para>Splits complete labelled data by class into 60% fitting, 20% validation and 20% test rows (per-class rounding applies). Four random widths followed by eight Gaussian-process expected-improvement proposals are the default search budget. Proposals in [min_hidden,max_hidden] are rounded to integer widths; repeated widths reuse their cached validation log loss. Smaller loss wins; ties retain the first proposal. Each candidate has one tanh hidden layer, softmax output, training-only standardization, SGD learning rate 0.05, batch size 32 and L2 penalty 0.0001. Initialization/shuffling use seed for every candidate.</para>
