  /// <summary>Classical (overlay) hierarchical B-spline in the style of Forsey and Bartels: every cell of a dyadic tree may carry its own local "detail" TensorBSpline.</summary>
  /// <remarks>
  /// <para>Wraps the C++ class <c>datamunge::fda::HierarchicalBSpline</c>.</para>
  /// <para>evaluate(x) sums the patch of every cell on the root-to-leaf path containing x. Each patch is evaluated in its cell's local coordinates, (x - cell_min) / (cell_max - cell_min) in [0, 1]^d, so patch bases should span [0, 1]. Patches are independent (no shared nested basis and no truncation); see TruncatedHierarchicalBSpline for the THB-spline construction. Cells are identified by integer ids (root 0).</para>
  /// <para><b>Example</b></para>
  /// <code>
  /// dm::fda::HierarchicalBSpline h({0.0}, {1.0});
  /// auto b = dm::fda::BSplineBasis::open_uniform(0, 1);              // constant patch
  /// h.set_spline(h.root(), dm::fda::TensorBSpline(b, {1.0}));
  /// h.refine(h.root(), 1, dm::fda::TensorBSpline(b, {2.0}));          // upper half
  /// std::print("{} {}\n", h.evaluate({0.25}), h.evaluate({0.75}));    // 1 3
  /// </code>
  /// <para><b>References</b></para>
