/// <summary>Asymptotic effective-sample-size fraction</summary>
/// <remarks>
/// <para>Calls C++ <c>datamunge::bayes::gaussian_importance_efficiency</c>.</para>
/// <para><c>N_{\text{eff}}/N</c> of importance sampling a <c>d</c>-dimensional Gaussian target with a Gaussian proposal of the same mean and covariance scaled by <c>k^2</c>.</para>
/// <para><c>N_{\text{eff}}/N\to1/E_q[w^2]</c> for weights <c>w=p/q</c> normalised to mean 1. In one dimension <c>E_q[w^2]=\int p^2/q=k^2/\sqrt{2k^2-1}</c>, finite only for <c>k^2&gt;1/2</c>, and the dimensions multiply, giving <c>\bigl(\sqrt{2k^2-1}/k^2\bigr)^d</c>. It is 1 at <c>k=1</c> and 0 (infinite weight variance) for <c>k\le1/\sqrt2</c>.</para>
