/// <summary>Makes sure a downloadable dataset is on disk and returns where it is.</summary>
/// <remarks>
/// <para>Calls C++ <c>datamunge::datasets::fetch</c>.</para>
/// <para>For tabular datasets this is the CSV file. UCI names such as "uci_53" and "uci_iris" point to the same cache. UCI verifies size and SHA-256 on every access and stages complete bytes before publishing them. For the image datasets it is a directory: "mnist" and "fashion_mnist" hold the four uncompressed IDX files (<c>train-images-idx3-ubyte</c>, ...); "cifar10" holds <c>data_batch_1..5.bin</c> and <c>test_batch.bin</c>; "cifar100" holds <c>train.bin</c> and <c>test.bin</c> (the binary versions); "sudoku" holds Norvig's <c>easy50.txt</c>, <c>top95.txt</c> and <c>hardest.txt</c>. "karate_club" holds the970-byte original ZIP, GML topology and source README; every cached archive/member is checksum-verified. karate_club() reads34nodes/78edges. "rebot_devarm" holds 38 pinned Seeed DevArm CAD/URDF/STL files and the CERN-OHL-W-2.0 source license in their upstream relative directory layout. DevArm verifies the size and SHA-256 of every cached file on every call; changed files throw without replacement. Missing files are staged and verified before publication. It uses the same offline/mirror/cache controls, and works without the optional native data-preparation dependencies. Hashing uses memory proportional to the largest source file (about 35 MB). Approximate download sizes: diamonds 2.7 MB, california_housing 1.4 MB, MNIST 11 MB, Fashion-MNIST 30 MB, CIFAR-10 163 MB, CIFAR-100 161 MB, sudoku 14 KB, DevArm 56 MB.</para>
/// <para><b>Example</b></para>
/// <code>
/// const auto housing = dm::datasets::read_csv(dm::datasets::fetch("california_housing"));
/// </code>
/// <para>For a complete CAD asset tree, use <c>dm::datasets::fetch("rebot_devarm")</c>.</para>
/// <para><b>References</b></para>
/// <list type="bullet">
/// <item><description>Seeed reBot-DevArm source: https://github.com/Seeed-Projects/reBot-DevArm</description></item>
/// </list>
/// <para>See also: <c>data_home()</c>, <c>downloadable()</c>, <c>download_file()</c>, <c>karate_club()</c>.</para>
/// <para>Leaves out the C++ default arguments <c>ADirectory = ''</c> (other overloads pass them).</para>
/// </remarks>
/// <param name="AName">One of downloadable() or a registered UCI alias.</param>
/// <returns>The local path of the CSV file or the dataset directory.</returns>
/// <exception cref="ENativeError">Kind <c>InvalidArgument</c> (C++ <c>std::invalid_argument</c>): for an unknown name.</exception>
/// <exception cref="ENativeError">Kind <c>Native</c> (C++ <c>std::runtime_error</c>): if files are missing and downloading is disabled or fails, or a download does not match its checksum.</exception>
function Fetch(const AName: String): String; overload;
