/// <summary>Construct a complete unconstrained Delaunay triangulation with exact signs. Retains the original one-vector signature and Triangle layout. Finite coordinate validation precedes even trivial results. Duplicates coalesce to earliest ids; collinear/fewer-than-three distinct sites return no faces. Uses Bowyer-Watson cavity replacement with symbolic hull ghosts, avoiding any finite super-triangle whose proximity could remove valid narrow faces. All orientation/incircle signs are exact for finite stored binary64, including subnormals/extreme scales. Cocircular ties retain existing faces under the ordering in DelaunayTrace. Faces are strictly CCW, contain no ghosts and reference original ids. Finite output order is canonical as documented on DelaunayTrace. No boundary constraints, holes, Steiner refinement or minimum-angle guarantee is supplied. Input unchanged; O(n log(n+1)+u^2 log(u+1)) worst-case work for n records/u distinct sites with ordered cavity maps and full live scans; O(n+u) working/output storage, no shared state or optional resource caps. Exact-predicate cost is bounded per binary64 query.</summary>
/// <remarks>
/// <para>Calls C++ <c>datamunge::geometry::delaunay_triangulation</c>.</para>
/// <para><b>Example</b></para>
/// <code>
/// std::print("{}\n",dm::geometry::delaunay_triangulation({{0,0},{1,0},{.5,.000001}}).size()); // 1
/// </code>
/// <para><b>References</b></para>
/// <list type="bullet">
/// <item><description>A. Bowyer (1981), Computing Dirichlet tessellations, Computer Journal 24(2),162–166, doi:10.1093/comjnl/24.2.162.</description></item>
/// <item><description>D. F. Watson (1981), Computing the n-dimensional Delaunay tessellation with application to Voronoi polytopes, Computer Journal 24(2),167–172, doi:10.1093/comjnl/24.2.167. This variant uses symbolic boundary faces, exact decoded-dyadic signs, earliest duplicate identities and ordered cavity edges.</description></item>
/// </list>
/// <para>See also: <c>delaunay_trace()</c>, <c>incircle_sign()</c>.</para>
/// </remarks>
/// <param name="APoints">Borrowed finite planar sites, possibly empty/duplicate/collinear.</param>
/// <returns>Owned complete finite mesh of the distinct sites' convex hull, or no faces for collinearity.</returns>
/// <exception cref="ENativeError">Kind <c>InvalidArgument</c> (C++ <c>std::invalid_argument</c>): Any nonfinite coordinate, even on short input.</exception>
/// <exception cref="ENativeError">Kind <c>LengthError</c> (C++ <c>std::length_error</c>): Counter arithmetic or container capacity exceeded.</exception>
/// <exception cref="ENativeError">Kind <c>Native</c> (C++ <c>std::logic_error</c>): Internal cavity topology invariant fails; no partial mesh returned.</exception>
/// <exception cref="ENativeError">Kind <c>Allocation</c> (C++ <c>std::bad_alloc</c>): Allocation fails.</exception>
function DelaunayTriangulation(const APoints: TArrayOfPoint2D): TArrayOfTriangle; overload;
/// <summary>Capture actual symbolic-boundary cavity transitions from the same solver. No replay. Full finite validation precedes the original-record cap and all allocation. max_tests bounds cumulative incircle plus hull-side calls, checked before each complete live-face scan. Trace entries charge one per insertion plus removed faces, boundary edges and added faces, including ghosts, checked before retaining the event. Points/maps/final output and temporary cavities are excluded from that entry count; caps do not bound bytes or wall time. Zero disables only an optional cap. O(sum cavity/event sizes) additional history, at worst O(u^2), beyond the ordinary solver. Failure returns no partial result.</summary>
/// <remarks>
/// <para>Calls C++ <c>datamunge::geometry::delaunay_trace</c>.</para>
/// <para><b>Example</b></para>
/// <code>
/// const auto t=dm::geometry::delaunay_trace({{0,0},{4,0},{4,4},{0,4},{2,2}},5,10);
/// std::print("{} {}\n",t.triangles.size(),t.work.incircle_tests+t.work.hull_side_tests); // 4 10
/// </code>
/// <para><b>References</b></para>
/// <list type="bullet">
/// <item><description>Bowyer (1981), doi:10.1093/comjnl/24.2.162; Watson (1981), doi:10.1093/comjnl/24.2.167; records the symbolic-boundary variant rather than a geometric replay.</description></item>
/// </list>
/// <para>See also: <c>DelaunayTrace</c>, <c>delaunay_triangulation()</c>.</para>
/// <para>Leaves out the C++ default arguments <c>AMaxPoints = 1000000</c>, <c>AMaxTests = 10000000</c>, <c>AMaxEntries = 1000000</c> (other overloads pass them).</para>
/// </remarks>
/// <param name="APoints">Finite original coordinates, unchanged.</param>
/// <returns>Owned points, original-id maps, finite mesh, actual events and work.</returns>
/// <exception cref="ENativeError">Kind <c>InvalidArgument</c> (C++ <c>std::invalid_argument</c>): Any nonfinite coordinate.</exception>
/// <exception cref="ENativeError">Kind <c>LengthError</c> (C++ <c>std::length_error</c>): Optional cap, count arithmetic or container capacity exceeded.</exception>
/// <exception cref="ENativeError">Kind <c>Native</c> (C++ <c>std::logic_error</c>): Internal cavity invariant fails.</exception>
/// <exception cref="ENativeError">Kind <c>Allocation</c> (C++ <c>std::bad_alloc</c>): Allocation fails.</exception>
