/// <para>Calls C++ <c>datamunge::stats::kruskal_wallis_test</c>.</para>
/// <para>Ranks the pooled observations with average ties and uses the chi-square(k-1) approximation. The usual exchangeability null is identical independent group distributions; a common-shape shift model permits a location interpretation. It is not an omnibus test for every possible distributional difference. Small groups can invalidate the approximation. O(N log N) work/O(N) space, no mutation, omission or shared state.</para>
/// <para><b>Example</b></para>
/// <code>
/// const auto h=dm::stats::kruskal_wallis_test({1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9},{3,3,3});
/// std::print("{:.1f}\n",h.statistic); // 7.2
/// </code>
/// <para><b>References</b></para>
/// <list type="bullet">
/// <item><description>https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/stats/html/kruskal.test.html</description></item>
/// </list>
/// <para>See also: <c>HypothesisTestResult</c>.</para>
/// </remarks>
/// <param name="AValues">Finite observations concatenated by group.</param>
/// <param name="AGroupSizes">At least two positive group sizes summing to values.size().</param>
/// <returns>statistic=H, parameter1=k-1 and upper-tail approximate p_value; no CI.</returns>
/// <exception cref="ENativeError">Kind <c>InvalidArgument</c> (C++ <c>std::invalid_argument</c>): Invalid groups, nonfinite input or all observations tied.</exception>
function KruskalWallisTest(const AValues: TArrayOfDouble; const AGroupSizes: TArrayOfInt64): THypothesisTestResult; overload;
