/// <returns>The fitted spline.</returns>
/// <exception cref="ENativeError">Kind <c>InvalidArgument</c> (C++ <c>std::invalid_argument</c>): On empty/mismatched inputs, invalid lambdas, or an axis with no more functions than <c>order</c>.</exception>
/// <exception cref="ENativeError">Kind <c>Native</c> (C++ <c>std::runtime_error</c>): If the penalized normal equations are singular.</exception>
function FitTensorPspline(const ABases: TArrayOfBSplineBasis; const APoints: TArrayOfArrayOfDouble; const AValues: TArrayOfDouble; const ALambdas: TArrayOfDouble): TTensorBSpline; overload;
/// <summary>Fits a tensor-product P-spline: least squares plus an anisotropic difference penalty, solving (B^T B + P) c = B^T y with P from tensor_difference_penalty().</summary>
